# The Airbus A380-841's checklists: this project's own, in its own words.
#
# **They are not taken from the aeroplane's flight manual.** No such
# manual was read to write them. What they follow is the ordinary
# practice for the type, in the order it is flown; the speeds and
# settings in them are this project's own figures, assets/figures/a380.xml,
# whose sources docs/ASSETS.md records, and the flight model itself
# wherever the model is what decides - a lever's gate, a flap's travel,
# an engine's idle.
#
#   phase NAME                       one of: before-start, taxi, take-off,
#                                    climb, cruise, descent, approach,
#                                    landing, after-landing
#   check PROPERTY OP VALUE TEXT...  an item the aircraft can see done
#   range PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT...  the same, where a band shows it done
#   confirm TEXT...                  an item only the pilot can see done
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/checklist.hpp owns the format.
#
# Four Trent 970-84s, numbered one to four from the left, with neither mixture
# nor propeller: they are read by their N1, twenty per cent at idle - lower
# than the Boeings' thirty - and a hundred wide open. The outboard pair,
# engines one and four, stand for all four here. The flaps are read in degrees
# rather than by their configuration handle: eight is configuration 1+F,
# seventeen is 2, twenty-six is 3 and thirty-two is full.

phase before-start
confirm Walk-round done, all doors shut, and both decks reported secure
confirm Auxiliary power units running, and the four engines to be started in turn
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Thrust levers at idle
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
check fcs/speedbrake-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Speedbrake lever in and stowed
confirm Parking brake set, beacon on, and the ground crew clear of all four engines

phase taxi
range propulsion/engine[0]/n1 18.0 40.0 Number one running, its thrust lever at idle
range propulsion/engine[3]/n1 18.0 40.0 Number four running, its thrust lever at idle
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 7.5 17.5 Take-off configuration set, eight to seventeen degrees
range fcs/pitch-trim-cmd-norm -0.35 0.35 Pitch trim set for the take-off weight
confirm Brakes checked as it first moves, and the body gear steering seen to work
check velocities/vc-kts <= 20.0 Taxi at no more than twenty knots; the wing is very wide

phase take-off
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 7.5 17.5 Configuration 2, seventeen degrees, its field length figured
check gear/gear-pos-norm >= 0.95 All five undercarriage legs down and locked
check propulsion/engine[0]/n1 >= 90.0 Number one at take-off thrust
check propulsion/engine[3]/n1 >= 90.0 Number four at take-off thrust
confirm Take-off briefed, transponder on, and the runway seen to be clear
check velocities/vc-kts >= 160.0 Rotate at 160 knots at the maximum take-off weight

phase climb
check gear/gear-pos-norm <= 0.05 Undercarriage up
check position/h-agl-ft >= 400.0 Climbing away from the runway
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up, the configuration clean
range velocities/vc-kts 240.0 330.0 Climb at 250 knots below ten thousand feet, then 320
check velocities/h-dot-fps >= 8.0 Going up at 500 feet a minute or better
confirm Landing lights off above ten thousand feet, and engine anti-ice as it is needed

phase cruise
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
check fcs/speedbrake-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Speedbrake stowed
range position/h-sl-ft 30000.0 43000.0 Level between FL300 and the ceiling of 43,000 feet
range velocities/mach 0.80 0.87 Cruising near Mach 0.85, inside the Mmo of 0.89
confirm Fuel moved between the tanks to hold the centre of gravity where it belongs

phase descent
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.50 Thrust levers back for the descent
range velocities/h-dot-fps -60.0 -5.0 Coming down between 300 and 3,600 feet a minute
range velocities/vc-kts 200.0 320.0 Down at 310 knots, and 250 below ten thousand feet
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps still up
confirm Altimeters set to the field's pressure passing the transition level
confirm Approach briefed, and both cabin decks told to make ready for landing

phase approach
check gear/gear-pos-norm >= 0.95 All five legs down and locked
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 7.5 32.0 Configuration taken one step at a time as the speed falls
range velocities/vc-kts 135.0 200.0 Slowing through the flap speeds to the approach speed
check fcs/speedbrake-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Speedbrake lever in
check position/h-agl-ft <= 3000.0 Below three thousand feet and settled on the path
confirm Ground spoilers armed, landing lights on, and the runway in sight

phase landing
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 25.5 32.0 Configuration 3 or full, twenty-six to thirty-two degrees
check gear/gear-pos-norm >= 0.95 All five legs down and locked
range velocities/vc-kts 132.0 150.0 Over the threshold at 138 knots at the landing weight
check position/h-agl-ft <= 70.0 Seventy feet and below, into the flare; the eyes ride high
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.15 All four thrust levers to idle as the flare begins

phase after-landing
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
check fcs/spoiler-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Ground and flight spoilers in
check fcs/speedbrake-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Speedbrake lever in
check propulsion/engine[3]/n1 <= 40.0 All four thrust levers at idle
check velocities/vc-kts <= 20.0 Clear of the runway and slowed to a taxi
confirm Transponder to standby, landing lights off, and the auxiliary power units on
